WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.728
You have felt a static shock from a door handle.

00:00:05.008 --> 00:00:09.694
Now imagine that spark hitting a circuit board, too small for you to see or feel.

00:00:10.294 --> 00:00:16.385
Electrostatic discharge, or ESD, can kill or weaken a chip with no visible mark.

00:00:16.665 --> 00:00:20.871
The board may pass testing today, then fail later in your customer's hands.

00:00:21.471 --> 00:00:25.436
Static builds up as people move, and as materials rub together.

00:00:25.716 --> 00:00:31.820
When a charged person or tool touches a sensitive part, that charge jumps across in an instant.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:37.379
Much smaller charges than the ones you can feel are enough to damage modern electronics.

00:00:37.979 --> 00:00:42.093
ESD protection works by giving that charge a safe path to earth.

00:00:42.373 --> 00:00:48.586
Furnisys ESD workstations do this with electrostatic laminate tops or ESD mats,

00:00:48.586 --> 00:00:51.496
plus wrist straps and grounding kits.

00:00:51.776 --> 00:00:54.520
It is simple insurance for every board you build.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:01.325
So if your team handles PCBs, sensors or chips, ESD control is not optional.

00:01:01.605 --> 00:01:03.154
Do you have it at every bench?

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:08.235
Comment below, and next, see ESD worktop versus ESD mat.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:13.080
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

